Congress is taking action to prevent a  threatened partial government shutdown  tomorrow the house plans to vote today  on a spending bill to pay the bills  until February 8th the Senate approved  the measure late last night without  adding the money that President Trump  demanded for border security Nancy  Cordes is on Capitol Hill Nancy it  sounds like they're playing a game of  kick the can again so here's a question  well the president still signed that  legislation if it reaches his desk  Republican lawmakers hope so in fact  they say they think the president is  going to sign this bill before tomorrow  night's deadline even though it doesn't  contain the wall funding that he had  been asking for it doesn't contain any  additional funding for building the  president's promised border wall just  last week remember he said he would be  proud to shut down the government if he  didn't get five billion dollars to  fulfill his signature campaign promise  but Democrats balked at even 1 billion  dollars in wall funding and Republicans  just can't pass a funding bill without  those Democratic votes so they've come  up with a compromise that is as you  noted Gale a temporary fix it keeps the  government funded but only through  February 8th which gives Republicans a  chance to bargain again for wall funding  in the new year most importantly what  this bill does is prevent a shutdown of  1/4 of the government tomorrow night  which would leave Gale about 400,000  federal employees furloughed right  before Christmas nobody wants that to  happen so what does this mean for the  president's border wall the wall by the  way which during the campaign he kept  saying Mexico was going to pay for it it  turned into a campaign chant right well  now he is looking for ways for the US  government to pay for it that don't  involve funding from Congress he says  he's not giving up in fact he tweeted  one way or the other we will win on the  wall and he has been asking federal  agencies to come up with this additional  money somehow instead and if that  doesn't work some Trump supporters are  taking things into their own hands gale  there is a one Iraq war veteran who  started a GoFundMe page for the wall a  few days ago and he's already raised  more than 2.5 million dollars  all right yeah I heard him say that if  every Trump voter gave $80 it would pay  for the wall we'll see Nancy thank you  very much
 

